<title>IRAN: Iran says red meat production at 690,000 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Iran says red meat production at 690,000 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran's red meat production has reached 690,000 tonnes a year, meeting 93 percent of the country's needs, an Iranian minister said in remarks published on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Construction Jihad Minister Gholamreza Forouzesh, quoted by the daily Ettelaat, also said Iran's 18,000 poultry farms produced 560,000 tonnes of chicken meat and 450,000 tonnes of eggs a year. Comparative figures for earlier years were not given.</p>
<p>Forouzesh said six large abattoirs were under construction, each with a daily capacity to slaughter 6,000 sheep and 700 cattle.</p>
</text>
